## Context

The ~/.idh layout was retired by the portable lifecycle (0987/0999, PR #1091);
the reference checkout is ~/.agents. The zotero-arch session (PR #1143) fixed one
such stale path in skills/ (probe-url.py docstring) — and the skills agnostic
gate caught the overcorrected bare form. But the gate's jurisdiction is
`skills/**` only: the same retirement has live survivors in `scripts/`, both
operator-facing, and the gate's own pattern comments recommend the retired
layout.

## Findings (origin/main @ 267cde2f)

- `scripts/census/README.md:21,25` — `C=~/.idh/scripts/census`,
  `--root ~/.idh`: an operator following the README runs against a path that no
  longer exists on this machine.
- `scripts/check-primary-checkout.sh:14` — comment documents `REPO_DIR`
  defaults to `$HOME/.idh`.
- `scripts/check-agnostic.sh:18,46` — the forbidden-pattern comments recommend
  `~/.idh/scripts/` (and `/home/[a-z]` advises "use ~/.idh"): the gate steers
  writers toward the retired layout.

## Actions

1. Census README: point at the harness checkout (`$IDH_ROOT/scripts/census`,
   `--root "$IDH_ROOT"`), keeping the agnostic-safe form.
2. check-primary-checkout.sh comment: state the actual default.
3. check-agnostic.sh pattern comments: recommend `$IDH_ROOT/scripts/` (or the
   `$HARNESS_DIR` form, see 1021-adjacent PR #1143 review) instead of ~/.idh.
4. Decide whether a scripts/-level equivalent of the skills agnostic gate is
   warranted, or record that scripts/ is out of its jurisdiction by design.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] No live `~/.idh` reference remains in scripts/ or the gate comments
      (historical docs and tickets untouched)
- [ ] The census README instructions run as written from a harness checkout
- [ ] make check-fast passes

## Test

- `grep -rn "\.idh" scripts/` returns only historical/provenance mentions, if any.
